    "title": "Concept: What is a Simple Molecular Substance?",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">A <strong>simple molecular substance</strong> is made up of molecules containing a small number of atoms covalently bonded together. Examples include <em>water (H<sub>2</sub>O)</em>, <em>carbon dioxide (CO<sub>2</sub>)</em>, and <em>methane (CH<sub>4</sub>)</em>. These substances are held together by <strong>strong covalent bonds</strong> within the molecules but the forces between molecules are much weaker.</p>",
